From bd9be6ed793aa313b0cfbd4e1dbf69c6231baf59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:32:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): the desktop gates pass again, so a desktop push
 needs no bypass

tests (15 failing, plus 2 that need a browser)
- electron-updater is loaded when the updater first needs it again. A refactor
  had made it a module-scope import in main/index.ts, which loads it on every
  dev launch; main-updater-wiring.test.ts was red on exactly that.
- Ten tests still described the code before the (required, optional) argument
  refactor: three preload subscribe pins, the theme-preview sender guard, a
  conversation-store fake, and four tests that run the TypeScript before-quit
  handler in a VM as if it were JavaScript (they now strip its types first).
- Five tests pinned words or a version that Jini owns. They hold for the
  pinned Jini release and for a linked Jini checkout: the two known wordings
  of a failure reason are both accepted, and the locked sidecar version is
  compared only with an installed copy.
- The two Chromium layout tests skip, in plain words, only on a machine with
  no Playwright browser. In CI a missing browser still fails them.

complexity (4 new violations): handleSiteControl, handleRename,
resolveSiteDir and smokeBridge are split into named helpers under the 9/9
ceiling. smokeBridge also drops from 72 lines to under 50.

coverage: jini-kits.ts and jini-surfaces.ts had no test loading them. Two
render tests now mount them the way main.tsx does and check the real
behaviour behind each binding; a mutation of any binding fails one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FiTZBnDLxeCuSHzGR9BTbQ
